  "dom_id": "step-q160280",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "What is the magnitude of the number $z=-9\\text{i}?$",
  "worked_solution": "The imaginary number $-9\\text{i}$ is equivalent to the complex number $z=0-9\\text{i}.$\n\nWe know that for a complex number $z=a+b\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, the magnitude of $z=0-9\\text{i}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|z| & =\\sqrt{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(0)^{2}+(-9)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{81} \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
